		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3023&amp;p=24317#p24317"><![CDATA[
How large is the duplex spacing ?<br><br>I've heard that you should have at least 5 MHz as the receiver part in the duplex hat otherwise will be swamped with RF from the transmitter <br>and have bad sensitivity.<br>This will affect 2 slot DMR as the hotspot and radio needs to synchronize the TS timing.<br><br>In Sweden we have only 432-438 MHz and the standard repeater shift is -2 MHz , and because of the bandplan it's not easy to get enough spacing.<br>I have a MMDVM_HS_Dual_Hat which is using 434.9375 TX and 432.9375 RX, this works fine with D-Star but not so good with DMR and I usually<br>get those TIMEOUT errors to as the sync is failing.<br>If I crank up the power on the OpenGD77 radios it usually work better but it's not 100% stable.<br><br>You can also get better results by separating the TX and RX antennas.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sun Jul 09, 2023 9:59 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
